            .permNetworkBody: "checking for updates and downloading them, plus the two optional helpers: the torrent engine and the 7-Zip archiver. that is the only server Hop talks to on its own.",
            .permTorrentTitle: "network — torrent traffic",
            .permTorrentBody: "only with the torrent module on: connections to other peers, exactly like any torrent client. nothing passes through us.",
            .permSpeedTitle: "network — speed test",
            .permSpeedBody: "the speed test runs macOS's own networkQuality tool, which measures against Apple's servers. no third-party service is involved.",
            .permAccessibilityTitle: "accessibility",
            .permAccessibilityBody: "three things need it: pasting into the app underneath (the clipboard's paste button), moving and resizing windows, and the keyboard lock. macOS governs all of them with this one switch.",
            .permMissingBody: "the keyboard lock, the window zones and the paste button need accessibility. if hop is already in the list with its switch on, that switch belongs to an older signature and grants nothing: remove hop with the minus button and add it again.",
            .permLostBody: "hop had accessibility and no longer has it. an update that changes hop's signature makes macOS drop it while the switch goes on looking on, and macOS does not ask again on its own: remove hop from the accessibility list with the minus button and add it again.",
            .permStaleTitle: "macOS lists hop as allowed, and it is not",
            .permStaleBody: "hop sent an event through and it reached the apps underneath, so nothing is being stopped. opening the switch is not enough here: remove hop from the accessibility list with the minus button and add it again.",
            .keylockBroken: "macOS switched the lock off and it would not stay on, so the keys are live again.",
            .permScreenTitle: "screen recording",
            .permScreenBody: "only the text recognition module, and only when it frames an area on screen: a frame means reading its pixels. a dropped or pasted picture needs nothing at all. Hop reads the rectangle you draw, when you ask for it, and nothing else. the eyedropper does NOT need this — the system loupe hands back a single color.",
            .permNotifyTitle: "notifications",
            .permNotifyBody: "the timer's alert when it finishes, and a note when a torrent completes. nothing else is ever posted.",
